1
00:00:01,466 --> 00:00:04,221
<i>Your selfish feelings</i>

2
00:00:04,221 --> 00:00:07,173
robbed me of the job I loved.

3
00:00:07,173 --> 00:00:09,185
Goodbye.

4
00:00:09,185 --> 00:00:11,266
I don't think we'll ever meet again.

5
00:00:16,245 --> 00:00:20,589
My love stole O-Con's love.

6
00:00:23,777 --> 00:00:27,600
What? Did you actually take that seriously?

7
00:00:30,501 --> 00:00:32,741
I mean, even with all
your aggressive advances,

8
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:37,205
did Ms. Kusakabe ever look
genuinely disgusted or creeped out?

9
00:00:37,205 --> 00:00:38,761
No.

10
00:00:38,761 --> 00:00:41,053
But I'm her employer, so in front of me...

11
00:00:41,053 --> 00:00:44,633
She never acted like that
in front of us either.

12
00:00:45,485 --> 00:00:46,845
Then why?

13
00:00:46,845 --> 00:00:49,185
- Why say something so harsh to me?
- Most likely,

14
00:00:49,185 --> 00:00:51,021
it was for Tuesla's sake.

15
00:00:51,021 --> 00:00:54,121
- Tuesla?
- Just like you and Mr. Omishima,

16
00:00:54,121 --> 00:00:56,833
Ms. Kusakabe is facing
a big scandal right now.

17
00:00:58,525 --> 00:01:00,233
[Arrest the Home Wrecker!
Ms. Kusakabe Only Cares About Clients' Money]

18
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:02,989
[Pure Evil: Target Kitchen Sakoda Destroyed!]

19
00:01:02,989 --> 00:01:04,881
These awful people!

20
00:01:04,881 --> 00:01:08,481
She probably felt that this scandal
was hurting Tuesla's revival,

21
00:01:08,481 --> 00:01:11,069
and so that's why she left.

22
00:01:12,701 --> 00:01:15,745
I'll tell her not to
pay any attention to that kind of stuff!

23
00:01:15,745 --> 00:01:18,705
Hold on a second!

24
00:01:18,705 --> 00:01:22,433
Don't you realize
why Ms. Kusakabe went so far

25
00:01:22,433 --> 00:01:24,656
as to make you hate her
with those harsh words?

26
00:01:24,656 --> 00:01:26,525
I know why.

27
00:01:26,525 --> 00:01:27,905
I'm not telling you, though.

28
00:01:27,905 --> 00:01:30,889
Because you'd try to drag her back like this!

29
00:01:30,889 --> 00:01:33,061
That won't change anything.

30
00:01:33,061 --> 00:01:38,033
<i>Unless we ease Ms. Kusakabe's anxiety,
she won't come back.</i>

31
00:01:40,881 --> 00:01:43,117
- Then what should I do?
- Until the scandal blows over,

32
00:01:43,117 --> 00:01:45,525
keep Tuesla's spark alive.

33
00:01:45,525 --> 00:01:50,929
Build up Tuesla so much
that Ms. Kusakabe feels safe coming back.

34
00:01:51,553 --> 00:01:53,045
And then...

35
00:01:53,045 --> 00:01:55,185
Marriage?

36
00:01:55,185 --> 00:01:57,601
- I don't know about that, but...
- I see.

37
00:01:57,601 --> 00:01:59,233
All right!

38
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:02,541
Just wait, O-Con!

39
00:02:02,541 --> 00:02:04,670
[Super! Good Mood Festival!]
<i>♪ Spring, Magic, Magic ♪</i>

40
00:02:04,670 --> 00:02:07,249
<i>♪ Stand up! Love and bow! Yeah! ♪</i>

41
00:02:07,249 --> 00:02:10,641
<i>♪ Three, two, one. Spring, Magic, Magic ♪</i>

42
00:02:10,641 --> 00:02:12,781
Try some Zapaan!

43
00:02:12,781 --> 00:02:16,621
One sip will wash your troubles away!
How about some Zapaan?

44
00:02:16,621 --> 00:02:19,885
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you!

45
00:02:19,885 --> 00:02:21,461
Nice!

46
00:02:21,461 --> 00:02:24,721
Your smile is so gentle, Ms. Kusakabe!

47
00:02:24,721 --> 00:02:26,333
In comparison...

48
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:27,669
This is Zapaan.

49
00:02:27,669 --> 00:02:30,521
- It'll improve your gut health...
- Hey, you!

50
00:02:30,521 --> 00:02:32,233
- You're way too stiff!
- Ah, wait...

51
00:02:32,233 --> 00:02:34,109
Your smile is as hard as a baguette!

52
00:02:34,109 --> 00:02:36,269
- Sorry.
- Soften it up!

53
00:02:36,269 --> 00:02:38,121
- Yes.
- Go on!

54
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:40,121
This is Japan! Uh...

55
00:02:40,121 --> 00:02:41,481
- This is Zapaan.
- What are you saying?

56
00:02:41,481 --> 00:02:43,205
- The power of lactic acid...
- More, more!

57
00:02:43,205 --> 00:02:44,866
- Swirl it all around!
- Go on! Zapaan!

58
00:02:44,866 --> 00:02:48,900
Ever since I closed the restaurant,
I've had nothing to do.

59
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,621
So I took a part-time job.

60
00:02:50,621 --> 00:02:51,745
Oh?

61
00:02:51,745 --> 00:02:54,165
You're not reopening the restaurant?

62
00:02:54,165 --> 00:02:56,677
Why not run it together
with your former wife as exes?

63
00:02:57,821 --> 00:02:59,589
[Learn Rosy Investment Tips]
She's no longer

64
00:02:59,589 --> 00:03:01,065
[from Ms. Sakoda]
the wife I knew.

65
00:03:01,065 --> 00:03:03,153
[Challengers Winning in the
Accelerating Business World]

66
00:03:03,153 --> 00:03:05,893
You didn't have to quit your job, though.

67
00:03:05,893 --> 00:03:07,345
Well...

68
00:03:07,345 --> 00:03:08,481
A lot happened.

69
00:03:08,481 --> 00:03:10,509
Because of the scandal, right?

70
00:03:10,509 --> 00:03:12,917
Go back once it blows over, okay?

71
00:03:12,917 --> 00:03:14,641
Seriously.

72
00:03:17,193 --> 00:03:20,545
What should we do
to stage Tuesla's big comeback?

73
00:03:20,545 --> 00:03:23,885
Create some friends for Tuesla.

74
00:03:23,885 --> 00:03:24,961
Friends?

75
00:03:24,961 --> 00:03:27,200
Like Mimmy for Hello Kitty,

76
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:30,433
or Nonnon for Sunsun.

77
00:03:40,521 --> 00:03:43,541
- Hello, this is Omishima Design.
- Seo Design!

78
00:03:45,337 --> 00:03:47,741
<i>How's the sales trip going?</i>

79
00:03:47,741 --> 00:03:51,989
Well, I visited shops all over Tokyo,

80
00:03:51,989 --> 00:03:55,613
but due to the scandal,
I haven't really gotten any good responses.

81
00:03:55,613 --> 00:03:56,697
<i>Tokyo?</i>

82
00:03:56,697 --> 00:04:00,025
Aren't you misunderstanding something,
Mr. Hirose?

83
00:04:00,025 --> 00:04:01,121
What do you mean?

84
00:04:01,121 --> 00:04:04,037
I didn't want you to go around Tokyo,

85
00:04:04,037 --> 00:04:09,389
<i>but to our cash cow nation
that's full of Mizuki Seo fans.</i>

86
00:04:09,389 --> 00:04:11,533
The Republic of Tektorian.

87
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:13,900
I'm on my way!

88
00:04:15,066 --> 00:04:19,057
Ms. Sasaoka, you're good at taking
candid sneaky photos, right?

89
00:04:19,057 --> 00:04:22,833
No, no, I wouldn't say I'm good at it.

90
00:04:31,366 --> 00:04:32,513
Like this?

91
00:04:32,513 --> 00:04:34,193
Oh, yeah, yeah.

92
00:04:34,193 --> 00:04:35,285
Okay, Mr. Seo,

93
00:04:35,285 --> 00:04:38,937
now gently place your hand
on Mr. Omishima's back.

94
00:04:38,937 --> 00:04:41,121
- Gently?
- Yes.

95
00:04:42,021 --> 00:04:44,089
Gently. Good, good.

96
00:04:44,089 --> 00:04:47,477
Ah, don't look at the camera.
It ruins the look of a candid, sneaky photo.

97
00:04:47,477 --> 00:04:48,929
Keep it natural.

98
00:04:48,929 --> 00:04:51,481
Now sit next to him
and put an arm around his shoulder.

99
00:04:51,481 --> 00:04:54,069
Great. Yes, very good. Thank you.

100
00:04:54,069 --> 00:04:57,393
Okay, Mr. Omishima, now please
do that fake cry that's your specialty.

101
00:04:57,393 --> 00:05:00,341
Nice. You're crying. You're crying.

102
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:03,517
Yes, now look like you're
full of regret. Deep regret.

103
00:05:03,517 --> 00:05:06,777
- I regret everything.
- Ah, you're even saying it!

104
00:05:06,777 --> 00:05:10,193
Even though it's a photo,
that remorse really comes through.

105
00:05:10,193 --> 00:05:13,521
A touching untold story:
Mizuki Seo reaches out

106
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:17,089
to save washed-up loser Omishima.

107
00:05:17,089 --> 00:05:19,553
Using my twenty burner accounts,

108
00:05:19,553 --> 00:05:21,893
- I'll hype up this story.
- Twenty?

109
00:05:21,893 --> 00:05:24,733
The tide will turn.

110
00:05:24,733 --> 00:05:25,733
[The handsome Mizuki Seo
saves the scandalous Mr. Omishima]

111
00:05:25,733 --> 00:05:26,817
[So heartwarming! Check out this article!]

112
00:05:26,817 --> 00:05:28,645
[Wow, Mr. Seo is so sweet!]
Amazing.

113
00:05:33,069 --> 00:05:36,137
- One, please.
- Thank you very much.

114
00:05:36,137 --> 00:05:38,433
Oh, Mr. Fuchinobe! What are you doing here?

115
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:40,893
I heard from Ms. Kominami.

116
00:05:40,893 --> 00:05:42,585
She said that you quit Seo Design,

117
00:05:42,585 --> 00:05:45,705
but you seem lingeringly attached.
[*Pun on "back-hair pulled" in Japanese]

118
00:05:45,705 --> 00:05:48,801
I'm not lingering at all.
My hair is silky smooth.

119
00:05:48,801 --> 00:05:52,637
So I wanted to help you out,

120
00:05:52,637 --> 00:05:55,137
and I went to gather some info on Seo Design.

121
00:05:57,765 --> 00:05:58,768
<i>Amazing.</i>

122
00:05:58,768 --> 00:06:01,269
- <i>Full of regret.</i>
- This is a glimpse of

123
00:06:01,269 --> 00:06:03,769
- <i>You're even saying it!</i>
- the Mizuki Seo Image Boost Campaign.

124
00:06:03,769 --> 00:06:07,673
Thanks to this, the backlash
is starting to die down.

125
00:06:07,673 --> 00:06:08,773
[Saving that trash Mr. Omishima?
What a huge heart!]

126
00:06:08,773 --> 00:06:09,905
[He really is a prince!]

127
00:06:09,905 --> 00:06:10,981
[I always knew he was a good guy deep down!]

128
00:06:10,981 --> 00:06:12,025
[So now that shady consultant is gone,
and Tuesla's back?]

129
00:06:12,025 --> 00:06:13,781
[Everyone flipped opinions, but leaving
that consultant was the right move]

130
00:06:14,909 --> 00:06:18,037
[Turns out he's actually a good guy]
What's with this pose?

131
00:06:18,037 --> 00:06:19,765
Is it trending?

132
00:06:24,873 --> 00:06:27,669
Just you wait, O-Con!

133
00:06:27,669 --> 00:06:29,761
O-Con?

134
00:06:29,761 --> 00:06:32,085
[O-Con]

135
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:37,805
He's coming.

136
00:06:37,805 --> 00:06:40,400
Once Tuesla makes a comeback,
he'll definitely...

137
00:06:41,617 --> 00:06:43,417
come.

138
00:06:44,777 --> 00:06:46,665
I have to move.

139
00:06:46,665 --> 00:06:48,837
I have to move before he comes.

140
00:06:48,837 --> 00:06:50,921
Oh! Ms. Kusakabe?

141
00:06:50,921 --> 00:06:55,609
- No, no, no!
- Is Kitchen Sakoda doing well?

142
00:06:58,485 --> 00:07:00,382
- Ms. Kumi.
- You've been visiting

143
00:07:00,382 --> 00:07:02,517
the main restaurant, right?

144
00:07:02,517 --> 00:07:06,281
It must be tough over there,
but it's tough here too.

145
00:07:06,281 --> 00:07:11,069
Talking about our divorce on TV like that.

146
00:07:11,069 --> 00:07:14,333
Because of that, my company
got dragged into a scandal too.

147
00:07:14,333 --> 00:07:16,600
Our sales plummeted.

148
00:07:17,941 --> 00:07:19,237
I'm so sorry.

149
00:07:19,237 --> 00:07:21,473
Are you going to take responsibility?

150
00:07:22,453 --> 00:07:23,469
Responsibility?

151
00:07:23,469 --> 00:07:25,366
Come on. Let's go.

152
00:07:27,085 --> 00:07:28,821
Mr. Taira,

153
00:07:28,821 --> 00:07:32,777
this woman was introduced by
our outside director, Ms. Kumi Sakoda,

154
00:07:32,777 --> 00:07:36,361
and has been appointed
as a consultant for Merry.

155
00:07:36,361 --> 00:07:38,573
Her name is Anna Kusakabe.

156
00:07:41,029 --> 00:07:44,566
Do your best. Just like you did for us.

157
00:07:57,721 --> 00:07:59,665
[Final Episode]

158
00:07:59,665 --> 00:08:01,833
I'm very sorry.

159
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:05,029
Swept along by Ms. Kumi's momentum,
I ended up coming here,

160
00:08:05,029 --> 00:08:08,509
[Wash your hands and gargle]
but me consulting for Merry is a bit...

161
00:08:08,509 --> 00:08:10,645
So regarding this matter...

162
00:08:11,249 --> 00:08:12,965
All right!

163
00:08:12,965 --> 00:08:15,837
- Ms. Kusakabe! Well...
- Oh, my God!

164
00:08:15,837 --> 00:08:19,361
My comment caused so much trouble.

165
00:08:19,361 --> 00:08:22,761
I am really, truly sorry!

166
00:08:22,761 --> 00:08:26,497
Well... Rena, you don't need to apologize.

167
00:08:26,497 --> 00:08:29,113
- Well then...
- Actually,

168
00:08:29,113 --> 00:08:32,253
ever since then,
our sales have been terrible.

169
00:08:32,253 --> 00:08:35,857
I thought our numbers would recover
if the president changed,

170
00:08:35,857 --> 00:08:38,579
but the new president basically just goes

171
00:08:38,579 --> 00:08:42,917
"Mmm..." all the time.

172
00:08:42,917 --> 00:08:46,873
- Listen, I really...
- Please, I beg you!

173
00:08:46,873 --> 00:08:49,449
Please save Merry.

174
00:08:49,449 --> 00:08:53,333
Well...

175
00:08:55,053 --> 00:08:58,889
We've already started restructuring staff

176
00:08:58,889 --> 00:09:01,797
and asking for voluntary resignations.

177
00:09:01,797 --> 00:09:06,093
If this keeps up,
we'll be looking at bankruptcy.

178
00:09:07,709 --> 00:09:11,817
By the way, if it comes to that,
what will happen to the characters?

179
00:09:11,817 --> 00:09:16,285
They'll likely all be
sold off before bankruptcy.

180
00:09:16,285 --> 00:09:19,245
Berry might sell,

181
00:09:19,245 --> 00:09:23,313
but the other characters
have almost no name recognition,

182
00:09:23,313 --> 00:09:26,277
so I don't know if anyone will buy them.

183
00:09:26,277 --> 00:09:28,713
And the same goes for Cynical Molco.

184
00:09:28,713 --> 00:09:31,766
With the bad reputation from the scandal,

185
00:09:31,766 --> 00:09:34,949
even lowering the price might not help.

186
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:39,117
And any unsold characters will never again...

187
00:09:39,117 --> 00:09:42,009
[Full Tummy Molco]

188
00:09:49,117 --> 00:09:54,766
Even if they're not famous,
or have a tainted image,

189
00:09:55,725 --> 00:09:58,133
there are still people who love them.

190
00:10:00,505 --> 00:10:04,217
There definitely are!

191
00:10:04,217 --> 00:10:09,161
And making people like those sad
is something that must never happen!

192
00:10:09,161 --> 00:10:11,433
Ms. Kusakabe...

193
00:10:11,433 --> 00:10:14,753
Let's do it! Let's revive Merry!

194
00:10:14,753 --> 00:10:19,866
For the characters,
and for the people who love them!

195
00:10:20,721 --> 00:10:25,441
[One Month Later]

196
00:10:35,601 --> 00:10:39,289
The tie-up contract for Tuesla is signed!

197
00:10:40,809 --> 00:10:43,245
[All Japan Heavy Industries,
Tie-up Commercial Proposal]

198
00:10:43,245 --> 00:10:45,885
A commercial at last.

199
00:10:45,885 --> 00:10:47,493
Iron Tuesla looks great.

200
00:10:47,493 --> 00:10:50,045
We finally made it this far
after that scandal.

201
00:10:50,045 --> 00:10:51,937
You're in the way.

202
00:10:51,937 --> 00:10:53,797
What? A trip? Trip-mishima?

203
00:10:53,797 --> 00:10:57,133
Explain it to him, Ms. Sasaoka. I'm busy.

204
00:10:57,133 --> 00:10:59,785
- He's going to Tektorian.
- Tektorian?

205
00:10:59,785 --> 00:11:03,661
There's a festival coming up soon,
celebrating their World Heritage fortress.

206
00:11:03,661 --> 00:11:06,266
It's called the Tektorian
Castle Hustle Carnival.

207
00:11:06,266 --> 00:11:07,633
He's going to attend that.

208
00:11:07,633 --> 00:11:09,993
Sightseeing, then! Giddy-mishima!

209
00:11:09,993 --> 00:11:12,845
Not at all! It's Work-mishima!

210
00:11:12,845 --> 00:11:16,757
One million tourists from
around the world attend this festival,

211
00:11:16,757 --> 00:11:18,489
and everyone gets hyped up.

212
00:11:18,489 --> 00:11:21,713
And at a festival like that...

213
00:11:21,713 --> 00:11:24,817
Wow, it's Tuesla! Castle Tuesla!

214
00:11:24,817 --> 00:11:26,889
Thanks to Mr. Hirose's PR efforts,

215
00:11:26,889 --> 00:11:28,965
as a new character
created by the same designer

216
00:11:28,965 --> 00:11:31,245
who came up with Cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho,
Tuesla is really popular.

217
00:11:31,245 --> 00:11:35,053
Despite having all the right conditions
in place to expand recognition,

218
00:11:35,053 --> 00:11:37,865
Mr. Hirose still can't speak
a word of Tektorian.

219
00:11:37,865 --> 00:11:39,557
So I am...

220
00:11:39,557 --> 00:11:41,393
Wait, you speak it?

221
00:11:41,393 --> 00:11:44,745
[*Speaking Tektorian]

222
00:11:45,857 --> 00:11:48,329
- What did you say?
- I'll leave the rest to you.

223
00:11:48,329 --> 00:11:51,013
I'll be counting on you.

224
00:11:51,013 --> 00:11:54,533
- Well...
- I was talking to Mr. Shiiba.

225
00:11:55,677 --> 00:11:57,513
Leave it to me.

226
00:11:57,513 --> 00:11:59,297
Well, then.

227
00:11:59,297 --> 00:12:01,166
Bring back some souvenirs.

228
00:12:09,297 --> 00:12:10,309
Man,

229
00:12:10,309 --> 00:12:12,341
[Seo Design New Character]
Tuesla is really taking off.

230
00:12:12,341 --> 00:12:13,733
[Tutu-Tuesla]
Indeed.

231
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:16,769
[Saying that a consultant]
Plus, Ms. Kusakabe's scandal,

232
00:12:16,769 --> 00:12:18,585
[caused my divorce]
ever since Ms. Kumi's post,

233
00:12:18,585 --> 00:12:20,713
[is an unacceptable accusation]
has pretty much cooled down.

234
00:12:32,865 --> 00:12:35,266
I think now's your chance.

235
00:12:42,065 --> 00:12:45,133
Just wait, O-Con!

236
00:12:50,237 --> 00:12:53,161
Hello, this is Sasaoka from Seo Design.

237
00:12:54,833 --> 00:12:56,721
What?

238
00:12:58,557 --> 00:13:00,193
It's from Merry.

239
00:13:00,193 --> 00:13:01,965
What?

240
00:13:18,109 --> 00:13:19,785
So about today's meeting...

241
00:13:19,785 --> 00:13:22,997
They want to discuss
Molco's future development

242
00:13:22,997 --> 00:13:26,329
with you as the creator.

243
00:13:26,329 --> 00:13:28,097
Oh.

244
00:13:28,825 --> 00:13:31,689
- What kind of discussion?
- As I said, details are...

245
00:13:31,689 --> 00:13:33,913
Thank you for waiting.

246
00:13:33,913 --> 00:13:37,505
Thank you for making time
to meet with us today.

247
00:13:38,125 --> 00:13:42,653
This is our president and CEO, Mr. Taira.

248
00:13:42,653 --> 00:13:44,697
Nice to meet you.

249
00:13:46,305 --> 00:13:48,033
In addition,

250
00:13:49,429 --> 00:13:51,393
the person handling this project,

251
00:13:51,393 --> 00:13:55,629
our consultant, Ms. Kusakabe,
will also be joining us.

252
00:13:55,629 --> 00:13:57,473
It's been a while.

253
00:14:01,913 --> 00:14:03,325
[Planning and Development Meeting]
Our company has decided

254
00:14:03,325 --> 00:14:07,309
to produce a new Cynical Molco movie.

255
00:14:07,309 --> 00:14:12,733
We hope to make it a sequel
that builds on the previous momentum.

256
00:14:12,733 --> 00:14:16,709
We have decided to have dual leads.

257
00:14:16,709 --> 00:14:19,393
One, of course, is Cynical Molco.

258
00:14:19,393 --> 00:14:21,281
And the other is this one.

259
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:24,089
Full Tummy Molco.

260
00:14:24,089 --> 00:14:26,129
In this film, Full Tummy Molco

261
00:14:26,129 --> 00:14:30,313
will appear as Cynical Molco's twin sister.

262
00:14:30,313 --> 00:14:32,113
[Dual Leads]
And for this film's director,

263
00:14:32,113 --> 00:14:35,769
we've brought in world-renowned Ryo Fukami,

264
00:14:35,769 --> 00:14:37,937
- with the screenplay by Yuiko Ninomaru...
- Well, excuse me...

265
00:14:37,937 --> 00:14:39,737
Well...

266
00:14:39,737 --> 00:14:41,137
Personally,

267
00:14:41,137 --> 00:14:46,869
I'm very glad to see Full Tummy Molco
finally see the light of day.

268
00:14:46,869 --> 00:14:49,221
But why so suddenly?

269
00:14:49,221 --> 00:14:53,217
Out of respect for you
as the designer, Mr. Seo,

270
00:14:53,217 --> 00:14:57,713
we reached out, hoping to get your input
in a supervisory role.

271
00:14:57,713 --> 00:14:59,509
Supervisor?

272
00:15:02,181 --> 00:15:05,166
Well... Mr. Seo?

273
00:15:06,557 --> 00:15:09,166
Mr. Seo. Mr. Seo.

274
00:15:09,829 --> 00:15:11,705
I get it!

275
00:15:11,705 --> 00:15:14,169
Revenge. That's it.

276
00:15:14,169 --> 00:15:17,245
You want to get back at Merry
for dragging Tuesla into a scandal

277
00:15:17,245 --> 00:15:19,049
- by destroying them from within...
- No.

278
00:15:19,049 --> 00:15:20,877
Wait, that's not it?

279
00:15:22,833 --> 00:15:24,673
Now I get it!

280
00:15:24,673 --> 00:15:26,900
Rehab. That's it.

281
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:29,417
You took a break from consulting,
so this is a warm-up

282
00:15:29,417 --> 00:15:31,133
- before coming back to us...
- No.

283
00:15:31,133 --> 00:15:33,300
I just accepted a normal client request.
That's all.

284
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:36,861
- Then what if we also hire you normally...
- Not possible.

285
00:15:36,861 --> 00:15:38,821
Huh? What?

286
00:15:38,821 --> 00:15:40,389
Mr. Seo. Mr. Seo?

287
00:15:40,389 --> 00:15:43,169
- Mr. Seo!
- You ditched us and quit,

288
00:15:43,169 --> 00:15:44,845
so why are you working
at Merry like nothing happened?

289
00:15:44,845 --> 00:15:46,765
It makes no sense! Am I wrong?

290
00:15:46,765 --> 00:15:49,467
- We're not talking about that...
- Yes, we are!

291
00:15:49,467 --> 00:15:51,685
What, you're a Merry person now?

292
00:15:51,685 --> 00:15:53,537
Has your brain gone all Merry too?

293
00:15:53,537 --> 00:15:55,733
You don't care about Tuesla at all, do you?

294
00:15:56,565 --> 00:16:00,105
We worked and worked and worked

295
00:16:00,105 --> 00:16:02,425
so you could feel safe coming back to us!

296
00:16:02,425 --> 00:16:04,801
And yet you betray us so casually!

297
00:16:04,801 --> 00:16:06,977
In the end,

298
00:16:06,977 --> 00:16:10,693
you never cared about Tuesla or Seo Design!

299
00:16:11,445 --> 00:16:13,265
- You're just totally half-hearted!
- I already told you

300
00:16:13,265 --> 00:16:15,133
why I quit Seo Design.

301
00:16:15,133 --> 00:16:17,181
Shall I say it again?

302
00:16:17,181 --> 00:16:21,549
Word for word,
the exact reason I gave that day.

303
00:16:21,549 --> 00:16:23,257
- Shall I repeat it right here?
- Well...

304
00:16:23,257 --> 00:16:25,061
Ms. Kusakabe?

305
00:16:28,757 --> 00:16:30,685
Do whatever you want.

306
00:16:31,749 --> 00:16:33,321
Not that I approve.

307
00:16:33,321 --> 00:16:34,501
Thank you.

308
00:16:34,501 --> 00:16:38,200
Moving forward, we will proceed
based on our own judgment.

309
00:16:40,765 --> 00:16:42,549
That's all.

310
00:16:59,365 --> 00:17:01,666
Excuse us. Excuse us.

311
00:17:08,465 --> 00:17:10,213
<i>How is Mr. Seo doing?</i>

312
00:17:11,229 --> 00:17:14,765
He's back to how he was
the day Ms. Kusakabe left.

313
00:17:14,765 --> 00:17:17,305
<i>Well, after being told that...</i>

314
00:17:17,305 --> 00:17:20,637
<i>Merry really is such a troublesome company.</i>

315
00:17:20,637 --> 00:17:22,234
<i>Well, you're the one who pushed them</i>

316
00:17:22,234 --> 00:17:24,285
<i>to the brink of bankruptcy, Mr. Omishima.</i>

317
00:17:24,285 --> 00:17:26,489
So, how are things over there?

318
00:17:26,489 --> 00:17:29,745
<i>Oh, it's amazing.</i>

319
00:17:29,745 --> 00:17:32,266
<i>The whole country is gearing up for
the Castle Hustle Carnival,</i>

320
00:17:32,266 --> 00:17:34,673
<i>and everyone here is ready to hustle!</i>

321
00:17:34,673 --> 00:17:37,437
<i>We can expect even higher profits
than anticipated.</i>

322
00:17:37,437 --> 00:17:38,593
Impressive as always.

323
00:17:38,593 --> 00:17:42,105
<i>Hey, why not bring Mr. Seo over here too?</i>

324
00:17:42,105 --> 00:17:43,845
<i>It'll cheer him up.</i>

325
00:17:43,845 --> 00:17:48,541
<i>Everyone's chanting, "Seo! Seo!"</i>

326
00:18:13,289 --> 00:18:15,121
Mugi!

327
00:18:21,113 --> 00:18:22,677
I see.

328
00:18:22,677 --> 00:18:26,945
So you're just trying to
protect Full Tummy Molco.

329
00:18:27,677 --> 00:18:33,089
Of course. I'm doing all this on my own,
and he doesn't know.

330
00:18:33,089 --> 00:18:35,800
Still, saying it like that...

331
00:18:37,889 --> 00:18:39,629
Anna,

332
00:18:40,301 --> 00:18:43,549
you really love Mr. Seo, don't you?

333
00:18:44,441 --> 00:18:46,617
Yeah.

334
00:18:46,617 --> 00:18:49,733
I think I do.

335
00:18:52,505 --> 00:18:53,877
I see.

336
00:18:53,877 --> 00:18:55,201
Sorry, I lied.

337
00:18:55,201 --> 00:18:57,077
Huh?

338
00:18:58,497 --> 00:19:01,545
I love him. I love him so much!

339
00:19:01,545 --> 00:19:03,709
Ah, okay.

340
00:19:03,709 --> 00:19:06,957
Even I myself don't really know why,

341
00:19:06,957 --> 00:19:09,937
but when I heard his war cry
at the proposal pitch,

342
00:19:09,937 --> 00:19:15,193
and when I heard that he'd turned down
the ambassador role, my heart fluttered.

343
00:19:15,193 --> 00:19:19,001
I told myself that for Tuesla's sake,
I couldn't fall for him,

344
00:19:19,001 --> 00:19:22,969
but seeing him and arguing with him today,

345
00:19:22,969 --> 00:19:27,133
all I could think was, "I love him!"

346
00:19:28,901 --> 00:19:32,713
Right now, if something were to happen,

347
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:35,701
I'd probably put Mr. Seo first,

348
00:19:35,701 --> 00:19:38,266
even if it meant sacrificing Tuesla.

349
00:19:39,537 --> 00:19:45,201
And Mr. Seo would probably do the same.

350
00:19:45,201 --> 00:19:47,200
Is that...

351
00:19:51,473 --> 00:19:53,209
Is that a bad thing?

352
00:19:53,209 --> 00:19:57,701
We're the ones who created Tuesla
to share with everyone,

353
00:19:57,701 --> 00:20:00,261
so we should prioritize Tuesla
above all else.

354
00:20:00,261 --> 00:20:02,189
We have that responsibility.

355
00:20:02,189 --> 00:20:06,737
Letting our feelings cloud that judgment

356
00:20:07,805 --> 00:20:10,289
is irresponsible,

357
00:20:10,289 --> 00:20:12,249
because we are its creators.

358
00:20:13,533 --> 00:20:17,100
Why don't you tell that to Mr. Seo?

359
00:20:22,369 --> 00:20:26,300
For everyone's sake...

360
00:20:27,409 --> 00:20:30,033
Is love really such a bad thing?

361
00:20:31,185 --> 00:20:34,765
I think your love

362
00:20:34,765 --> 00:20:37,817
and the love from the person
who taught you how to love

363
00:20:37,817 --> 00:20:39,749
are both wonderful.

364
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:56,453
You can't handle alcohol.

365
00:20:56,453 --> 00:20:58,905
The last one, number 100!

366
00:21:02,297 --> 00:21:05,529
[Can't Stop Pasta Snack]

367
00:21:07,081 --> 00:21:08,945
Excuse me, could you ring these up?

368
00:21:08,945 --> 00:21:11,393
- Welcome... Huh?
- Huh?

369
00:21:11,393 --> 00:21:14,681
Ah, are you working a gap part-time job?

370
00:21:15,757 --> 00:21:17,413
I see.

371
00:21:17,413 --> 00:21:19,429
[Can't Stop Pasta Snack]

372
00:21:19,429 --> 00:21:21,709
- Ah...
- No, no.

373
00:21:25,109 --> 00:21:29,766
Actually, Kumi came to the shop...

374
00:21:36,041 --> 00:21:37,853
There you are.

375
00:21:39,541 --> 00:21:41,893
I'll go grab some bags.

376
00:21:41,893 --> 00:21:44,893
Oh, no, I...

377
00:21:57,557 --> 00:21:59,437
I'm sorry.

378
00:22:01,657 --> 00:22:02,853
No...

379
00:22:02,853 --> 00:22:07,189
I was the one getting emotional
and saying rude things during work...

380
00:22:07,189 --> 00:22:08,781
Not for that.

381
00:22:08,781 --> 00:22:10,677
I'm saying sorry for...

382
00:22:13,693 --> 00:22:15,577
I'm sorry for falling in love with you.

383
00:22:17,421 --> 00:22:22,866
My love pulled you away
from the things you love.

384
00:22:25,633 --> 00:22:26,989
- Well...
- I mean,

385
00:22:26,989 --> 00:22:29,081
you love Tuesla so much.

386
00:22:29,893 --> 00:22:33,349
You still love and rely on it so much.

387
00:22:33,349 --> 00:22:39,133
Yet I confessed my feelings
and made you quit your job.

388
00:22:41,593 --> 00:22:43,381
I'm sorry.

389
00:22:46,605 --> 00:22:48,385
I won't say it anymore.

390
00:22:49,125 --> 00:22:51,941
I'll never talk about love or marriage again.

391
00:22:51,941 --> 00:22:54,025
In fact, I'll forget it.

392
00:22:54,025 --> 00:22:55,861
I'll act like none of it happened.

393
00:22:57,113 --> 00:22:59,809
So that's why we can do this.

394
00:22:59,809 --> 00:23:03,073
- I can supervise the movie.
- Huh?

395
00:23:03,073 --> 00:23:07,501
I know you care deeply
about Full Tummy Molco,

396
00:23:08,233 --> 00:23:10,673
and Molco is my responsibility.

397
00:23:10,673 --> 00:23:14,133
Besides, honestly, that premise was boring.

398
00:23:14,133 --> 00:23:17,833
- Boring...
- So business is business.

399
00:23:17,833 --> 00:23:21,589
Let's leave feelings out of it.

400
00:23:21,589 --> 00:23:23,713
In short...

401
00:23:23,713 --> 00:23:25,766
I look forward to working with you.

402
00:23:33,393 --> 00:23:36,233
Yes, likewise.

403
00:23:36,233 --> 00:23:38,509
I look forward to working with you.

404
00:23:38,509 --> 00:23:41,809
- So we have a deal?
- Yes.

405
00:23:41,809 --> 00:23:44,433
- Let's sign.
- Sign...

406
00:23:56,021 --> 00:23:58,121
Yeah.

407
00:23:58,121 --> 00:24:00,541
No tingling spark when we touch anymore.

408
00:24:08,493 --> 00:24:11,381
See you.

409
00:24:11,381 --> 00:24:13,249
Okay.

410
00:24:18,657 --> 00:24:22,133
It's tingling...

411
00:24:27,437 --> 00:24:29,761
[So love doesn't need a correct answer]

412
00:24:31,361 --> 00:24:32,453
- How is it?
- Well,

413
00:24:32,453 --> 00:24:35,297
- it's boring.
- Boring... What?

414
00:24:35,297 --> 00:24:38,457
You told me to give honest feedback.

415
00:24:38,457 --> 00:24:41,245
Still, as a consultant,
shouldn't you sugarcoat it

416
00:24:41,245 --> 00:24:43,266
to motivate the other person?

417
00:24:43,266 --> 00:24:45,329
Then do you really think this premise

418
00:24:45,329 --> 00:24:47,593
for Cynical Molco
and Full Tummy Molco isn't boring?

419
00:24:48,581 --> 00:24:50,713
But compared to the one
you came up with the other day,

420
00:24:50,713 --> 00:24:52,829
it's not exactly not-not-boring.

421
00:24:52,829 --> 00:24:54,329
- Not not-not-boring.
- Huh?

422
00:24:54,329 --> 00:24:57,297
Mine's more not-boring...

423
00:24:57,297 --> 00:24:58,829
Too many 'nots.' And you stumbled.

424
00:24:58,829 --> 00:25:02,009
- Twelve...
- One more time.

425
00:25:02,009 --> 00:25:03,721
This way.

426
00:25:05,105 --> 00:25:08,301
Can this place not even afford
security guards?

427
00:25:08,301 --> 00:25:10,333
Any suspicious person can just waltz in.

428
00:25:10,333 --> 00:25:12,805
Aren't you supposed to be in Tektorian?

429
00:25:12,805 --> 00:25:15,998
Actually, a huge crisis
has occurred in Tektorian.

430
00:25:15,998 --> 00:25:19,577
- Mr. Shiiba, hurry and get ready.
- Yes, sir.

431
00:25:19,577 --> 00:25:22,133
Wait, what's going on?

432
00:25:28,277 --> 00:25:30,621
I'm so glad you're safe.

433
00:25:30,621 --> 00:25:31,725
<i>Yeah.</i>

434
00:25:31,725 --> 00:25:33,885
<i>Wait, Ms. Kusakabe?</i>

435
00:25:33,885 --> 00:25:35,066
<i>Where are you right now?</i>

436
00:25:35,066 --> 00:25:38,169
Well, they said there was an accident...

437
00:25:38,169 --> 00:25:41,733
<i>The fortress suddenly collapsed.</i>

438
00:25:43,349 --> 00:25:44,945
<i>Can you see? Well...</i>

439
00:25:44,945 --> 00:25:48,389
<i>It looked like it could crumble
at any moment anyway,</i>

440
00:25:48,389 --> 00:25:51,553
<i>but the people of Tektorian are so laid-back.</i>

441
00:25:51,553 --> 00:25:53,549
<i>And well, being that way,</i>

442
00:25:53,549 --> 00:25:57,081
<i>safety measures fell behind,
and this happened.</i>

443
00:25:57,081 --> 00:25:59,485
Then what about the Castle Hustle Carnival?

444
00:25:59,485 --> 00:26:01,700
It's canceled, of course.

445
00:26:02,693 --> 00:26:05,985
<i>The locals were really looking forward to it,</i>

446
00:26:05,985 --> 00:26:09,461
<i>so everyone is in shock,
and the whole country feels gloomy.</i>

447
00:26:09,461 --> 00:26:12,221
As for the Tuesla shipments
that we'd planned for them,

448
00:26:12,221 --> 00:26:14,933
they won't be in the mood
to buy luxury goods for a while,

449
00:26:14,933 --> 00:26:16,965
so please cancel all orders.

450
00:26:16,965 --> 00:26:18,689
Understood.

451
00:26:20,925 --> 00:26:22,641
What are you doing?

452
00:26:23,321 --> 00:26:26,733
We're sending plushies. For free.

453
00:26:26,733 --> 00:26:28,433
What do you mean, for free?

454
00:26:28,433 --> 00:26:30,229
There are people there

455
00:26:30,889 --> 00:26:35,861
who love Seo Design's characters
and were looking forward to them.

456
00:26:35,861 --> 00:26:38,325
Right now, those people are feeling down.

457
00:26:38,325 --> 00:26:39,565
That's exactly when they need Tuesla!

458
00:26:39,565 --> 00:26:41,705
Is that really what they need?

459
00:26:42,349 --> 00:26:45,981
What they need right now is repair funds,

460
00:26:45,981 --> 00:26:49,021
heavy machinery, and manpower, isn't it?

461
00:26:49,021 --> 00:26:50,913
That may be true, but...

462
00:26:57,613 --> 00:26:59,433
Let's send them.

463
00:27:02,501 --> 00:27:04,549
Ah, sorry, I'm an outsider, but...

464
00:27:04,549 --> 00:27:06,369
Go on.

465
00:27:07,225 --> 00:27:11,113
Of course, money is extremely important.

466
00:27:11,113 --> 00:27:15,057
However, when you're about to give up,

467
00:27:15,693 --> 00:27:21,493
the things that support you
can be many things besides money, right?

468
00:27:21,493 --> 00:27:27,005
Like sports, songs,
favorite idols, characters,

469
00:27:27,005 --> 00:27:30,613
or support from strangers
whom you've never met.

470
00:27:31,257 --> 00:27:37,001
And right now, Seo Design can send Tuesla.

471
00:27:37,001 --> 00:27:40,789
You can send Tuesla
to people who are hurting.

472
00:27:40,789 --> 00:27:42,881
So shouldn't you do it?

473
00:27:42,881 --> 00:27:48,005
I'm sure Tuesla will give them strength.

474
00:27:48,901 --> 00:27:51,473
All right, let's do it!

475
00:27:51,473 --> 00:27:54,177
- Send all our stock to Tektorian!
- That's 500 plushies.

476
00:27:54,177 --> 00:27:56,261
Only 500? We can do more!

477
00:27:56,261 --> 00:27:58,765
- But...
- Sending more than that for free

478
00:27:58,765 --> 00:28:01,461
will harm Seo Design's operations.

479
00:28:01,461 --> 00:28:05,357
Five hundred is our absolute limit.

480
00:28:05,357 --> 00:28:08,329
No, that's nowhere near enough...

481
00:28:11,065 --> 00:28:13,600
Well... What is it?

482
00:28:16,933 --> 00:28:21,265
Can Merry help with that too?

483
00:28:23,066 --> 00:28:25,645
Can Merry help with that too?

484
00:28:25,645 --> 00:28:29,393
He actually spoke. Twice, even.

485
00:28:30,349 --> 00:28:33,166
Still, we don't have that kind of budget.

486
00:28:33,166 --> 00:28:36,466
We may lack budget,
but we still have inventory.

487
00:28:37,133 --> 00:28:42,609
So rather than having our characters
sleep in a warehouse...

488
00:28:42,609 --> 00:28:44,041
That's cool.

489
00:28:44,041 --> 00:28:45,809
But even so,

490
00:28:45,809 --> 00:28:49,161
that won't be enough
to reach all of Tektorian.

491
00:28:56,281 --> 00:29:00,233
Then why don't we get
more companies like this?

492
00:29:00,233 --> 00:29:01,409
Like this?

493
00:29:01,409 --> 00:29:04,057
There's a limit to what we can do alone,

494
00:29:04,057 --> 00:29:08,341
but if more companies like Merry pitch in,
we can make it happen.

495
00:29:08,341 --> 00:29:09,981
We can send plushies to all of Tektorian!

496
00:29:09,981 --> 00:29:11,721
But how?

497
00:29:11,721 --> 00:29:13,945
We just have to ask them!

498
00:29:13,945 --> 00:29:16,717
Ask them to send characters together
and support Tektorian!

499
00:29:16,717 --> 00:29:18,649
Every single character company out there!

500
00:29:18,649 --> 00:29:22,125
<i>Wait, you mean asking other companies?</i>

501
00:29:22,125 --> 00:29:24,533
Is that a bad thing? Why not?

502
00:29:24,533 --> 00:29:27,966
No, I think it's wonderful.

503
00:29:28,793 --> 00:29:32,133
Let's do it. Let's reach out!

504
00:29:33,537 --> 00:29:37,533
All right, things are about to get busy!

505
00:29:40,301 --> 00:29:42,161
All right!

506
00:29:46,325 --> 00:29:47,485
[Sent]
I just sent it.

507
00:29:47,485 --> 00:29:49,265
Print it out and hand it to everyone.

508
00:29:49,265 --> 00:29:51,433
Got it! Leave it to me!

509
00:29:52,977 --> 00:29:56,141
The news about the collapsed fortress
in the Republic of Tektorian.

510
00:29:56,141 --> 00:29:57,589
Ah, have you heard about that?

511
00:29:57,589 --> 00:30:01,801
For the Republic of Tektorian,
please lend us your support.

512
00:30:01,801 --> 00:30:04,233
Yes, thank you for your time.

513
00:30:14,337 --> 00:30:18,941
[Project Support The Republic of Tektorian]
Chara Palette.

514
00:30:18,941 --> 00:30:22,909
How many discontinued plushies
do you have left?

515
00:30:22,909 --> 00:30:25,633
We'd like to use them for relief aid
in the Republic of Tektorian.

516
00:30:25,633 --> 00:30:29,361
Could you please donate plushies
and cheering merchandise

517
00:30:29,361 --> 00:30:31,673
to the Republic of Tektorian?

518
00:30:33,117 --> 00:30:36,461
That's a pretty tough ask.

519
00:30:37,205 --> 00:30:39,169
Funassyi,

520
00:30:39,169 --> 00:30:41,545
before, when I came home
feeling down in the dumps,

521
00:30:41,545 --> 00:30:43,097
I saw you on TV,

522
00:30:43,097 --> 00:30:45,857
and found myself smiling
without even realizing it.

523
00:30:45,857 --> 00:30:49,809
And right now, Tektorian needs
your power, Funassyi! Please!

524
00:30:49,809 --> 00:30:53,000
Won't you lend us a hand?

525
00:30:54,789 --> 00:30:56,501
All right!

526
00:30:56,501 --> 00:30:58,445
Let Funassyi help out too!

527
00:30:58,445 --> 00:30:59,509
Thank you so much!

528
00:30:59,509 --> 00:31:01,700
You can count on me!

529
00:31:06,577 --> 00:31:08,333
Where should this go?

530
00:31:13,405 --> 00:31:14,557
[Kazuo Nimura: Dear Ms. Kusakabe,
this is Kazuo Nimura from Peace Plus]

531
00:31:14,557 --> 00:31:15,613
[Regarding the aid
you inquired about earlier,]

532
00:31:15,613 --> 00:31:17,865
[could our private jet be of any assistance?]

533
00:31:17,865 --> 00:31:23,600
Mr. Nimura from Peace Plus
just offered the use of his private jet!

534
00:31:26,021 --> 00:31:28,685
[Project Support The Republic of Tektorian]

535
00:31:30,053 --> 00:31:32,257
Wait! That label is way too crooked!

536
00:31:32,257 --> 00:31:33,973
It's not crooked at all! Where is it crooked?

537
00:31:33,973 --> 00:31:35,033
- It's so diagonal
- Come on!

538
00:31:35,033 --> 00:31:36,157
- you can't even read the letters!
- Stop it, you two!

539
00:31:36,157 --> 00:31:38,009
- Cut it out. All right, all right.
- Look, look!

540
00:31:38,009 --> 00:31:39,137
Snacks, snacks!

541
00:31:39,137 --> 00:31:41,725
- I brought you some snacks!
- Thank you very much.

542
00:31:41,725 --> 00:31:43,433
That one's completely off too! Redo it!

543
00:31:43,433 --> 00:31:45,513
Honestly, Mr. Seo, you're
obsessing over the labels

544
00:31:45,513 --> 00:31:46,557
- and barely making any
- Aren't those two

545
00:31:46,557 --> 00:31:47,644
- progress at all!
- dating?

546
00:31:47,644 --> 00:31:49,069
- Right?
- I'm putting my heart into it!

547
00:31:49,069 --> 00:31:50,705
- Fine! We're through!
- Apparently,

548
00:31:50,705 --> 00:31:52,361
- that's what they decided.
- If we're through, then we're through!

549
00:31:52,361 --> 00:31:54,713
As long as it brings happiness
to the people of Tektorian.

550
00:31:54,713 --> 00:31:55,845
It will!

551
00:31:55,845 --> 00:31:57,325
Because straight labels bring more joy!

552
00:31:57,325 --> 00:31:59,866
Way more joy than crooked ones do!

553
00:32:12,097 --> 00:32:17,017
[Always Together]

554
00:32:24,697 --> 00:32:26,217
Please take care of this.

555
00:32:26,217 --> 00:32:29,205
[Tektorian Castle Hustle Carnival, Cancelled]

556
00:33:01,929 --> 00:33:04,417
- Tuesla!
- Tuesla!

557
00:33:04,417 --> 00:33:07,585
- Tuesla!
- Tuesla!

558
00:33:07,585 --> 00:33:09,613
- Tuesla!
- All right!

559
00:33:09,613 --> 00:33:11,589
- Tuesla!
- Amazing!

560
00:33:11,589 --> 00:33:13,469
Tuesla!

561
00:33:13,469 --> 00:33:15,733
Tuesla!

562
00:33:47,681 --> 00:33:50,601
I was just thinking of heading out
to get some breakfast.

563
00:33:50,601 --> 00:33:52,566
I was thinking the same thing.

564
00:33:54,013 --> 00:33:55,793
Well, then...

565
00:33:58,066 --> 00:34:01,033
- Ah, how about this?
- Looks good.

566
00:34:07,285 --> 00:34:08,377
Welcome.

567
00:34:08,377 --> 00:34:10,781
Oh, you're working today too?

568
00:34:11,705 --> 00:34:14,566
Man, you sure eat a lot.

569
00:34:16,657 --> 00:34:18,849
[Can't Stop Pasta Snack]

570
00:34:21,897 --> 00:34:24,433
Excuse me, could you add this too?

571
00:34:27,313 --> 00:34:29,385
You know,

572
00:34:29,385 --> 00:34:34,269
ever since I was young,
it was always cooking, cooking...

573
00:34:34,269 --> 00:34:37,577
Just focused on making delicious meals.

574
00:34:37,577 --> 00:34:39,300
But she...

575
00:34:40,277 --> 00:34:44,317
Ever since Kumi met you,

576
00:34:44,317 --> 00:34:47,969
she started talking about money all the time.

577
00:34:47,969 --> 00:34:52,297
And one day, she told me

578
00:34:52,949 --> 00:34:58,869
not to obsess so much over
the restaurant and the flavor of its food.

579
00:34:58,869 --> 00:35:02,665
I thought, "It's over."

580
00:35:02,665 --> 00:35:08,977
I got stubborn, thinking that I had to
protect the restaurant on my own.

581
00:35:08,977 --> 00:35:10,877
And then...

582
00:35:13,549 --> 00:35:15,629
I lost her,

583
00:35:15,629 --> 00:35:20,009
and in the end, I even lost the restaurant.

584
00:35:21,973 --> 00:35:26,233
[Can't Stop Pasta Snack]
I wonder what I was even trying to protect.

585
00:35:31,685 --> 00:35:37,093
But then the other day,
Kumi came by the restaurant.

586
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:38,941
What?

587
00:35:39,697 --> 00:35:44,865
Before it closes,
I wanted to come see it one last time.

588
00:35:46,617 --> 00:35:53,021
<i>And she told me that just like me,</i>

589
00:35:53,021 --> 00:35:59,266
<i>she loved the restaurant,
and she loved its food.</i>

590
00:35:59,953 --> 00:36:02,257
<i>I was stunned.</i>

591
00:36:02,257 --> 00:36:05,521
Because she never gave any hint of that.

592
00:36:05,521 --> 00:36:11,213
In fact, she said the exact opposite.

593
00:36:21,637 --> 00:36:25,066
How people really feel

594
00:36:26,097 --> 00:36:31,397
isn't something you can easily figure out.

595
00:36:33,565 --> 00:36:36,673
Ah, sorry for rambling on about myself
out of nowhere like that.

596
00:36:36,673 --> 00:36:38,413
Not at all.

597
00:36:45,341 --> 00:36:47,237
All right.

598
00:36:49,777 --> 00:36:53,577
[Project Support The Republic of Tektorian]

599
00:36:53,577 --> 00:36:57,745
[Led by Tuesla,
Tektorian Relief Efforts Expand]

600
00:37:02,273 --> 00:37:03,969
Good morning.

601
00:37:03,969 --> 00:37:07,800
Look, Mr. Seo.
Look at all these letters from Tektorian.

602
00:37:10,977 --> 00:37:16,733
I have no idea what they say,
but I'm sure they're thrilled.

603
00:37:18,617 --> 00:37:21,033
Hey, O-Con,

604
00:37:21,033 --> 00:37:23,485
lately you've been here
every single day, haven't you?

605
00:37:23,485 --> 00:37:26,966
Ah, yes, ever since setting up headquarters.

606
00:37:28,101 --> 00:37:31,813
Commuting feels like a waste of time,

607
00:37:31,813 --> 00:37:37,045
and I feel like there's a more efficient way.

608
00:37:37,737 --> 00:37:40,700
Wait, do you mean...

609
00:37:40,700 --> 00:37:43,566
Ah, well, I mean...

610
00:37:44,881 --> 00:37:46,700
Yes, exactly that.

611
00:37:48,769 --> 00:37:50,877
I'm so happy!

612
00:37:50,877 --> 00:37:53,353
So happy!

613
00:37:53,353 --> 00:37:55,085
Then marry...

614
00:37:58,721 --> 00:38:01,253
I've wanted this forever!

615
00:38:01,253 --> 00:38:04,366
Then I can glide around smoothly!

616
00:38:04,973 --> 00:38:07,833
You're a consultant, O-Con.

617
00:38:07,833 --> 00:38:11,666
Isn't a consultant's job
to read people's feelings?

618
00:38:11,666 --> 00:38:13,973
Well, that's one aspect of it.

619
00:38:13,973 --> 00:38:16,733
But you have zero sense for that.

620
00:38:17,417 --> 00:38:19,533
Are you trying to irritate me again?

621
00:38:19,533 --> 00:38:23,921
Your misinterpretations
are way worse than mine.

622
00:38:23,921 --> 00:38:25,200
No, they're not.

623
00:38:25,200 --> 00:38:27,169
Even if I am bad at interpreting things,
at the very least,

624
00:38:27,169 --> 00:38:29,145
I'm definitely not worse than you.

625
00:38:29,145 --> 00:38:31,837
Oh, really? Is that so?

626
00:38:31,837 --> 00:38:35,697
I can read someone's feelings
after just talking to them a little bit.

627
00:38:35,697 --> 00:38:37,221
Oh, is that so?

628
00:38:37,221 --> 00:38:38,645
Well, I don't even need words.

629
00:38:38,645 --> 00:38:41,745
Just by looking at their face,
I know if they want to eat pineapple.

630
00:38:41,745 --> 00:38:44,229
Just from their face? Color me shocked.

631
00:38:44,229 --> 00:38:45,717
All right then, what about this face?

632
00:38:45,717 --> 00:38:47,933
What do you think I'm thinking? Go on.

633
00:38:48,833 --> 00:38:51,493
Yes, I've got it! You want to eat
some Giant Cheap Bread Taro!

634
00:38:51,493 --> 00:38:55,033
Wrong! The correct answer was,
"I want to get married."

635
00:38:56,657 --> 00:38:59,477
I won. I'm the real consultant.

636
00:38:59,477 --> 00:39:04,633
I'm Mizuki Seo-sultant...

637
00:39:07,857 --> 00:39:09,549
I'm sorry.

638
00:39:09,549 --> 00:39:12,353
No, wait. Talking to Mr. Sakoda earlier

639
00:39:12,353 --> 00:39:14,033
just made me feel kind of nostalgic.

640
00:39:14,033 --> 00:39:17,200
Anyway, my bad. I'm sorry.

641
00:39:19,569 --> 00:39:21,757
Huh?

642
00:39:21,757 --> 00:39:26,561
Huh? No, you calling yourself a consultant
is what really shocks me.

643
00:39:26,561 --> 00:39:27,925
I said, I'm sorry.

644
00:39:27,925 --> 00:39:31,166
Then what about this face?
What am I thinking right now?

645
00:39:33,117 --> 00:39:36,465
"How dare he talk about love
and marriage again! I'm furious!"

646
00:39:36,465 --> 00:39:37,645
Wrong.

647
00:39:37,645 --> 00:39:39,533
It's my "I want to get married too" face.

648
00:39:39,533 --> 00:39:42,766
I win. I'm the consultant, the Kabe-sultant!

649
00:39:47,549 --> 00:39:49,766
And this is...

650
00:39:51,297 --> 00:39:54,200
my "but I'm still anxious" face.

651
00:39:56,413 --> 00:40:01,129
Your grandma once told me that love is so big

652
00:40:01,129 --> 00:40:05,200
that if you keep holding it,
something will definitely spill over.

653
00:40:06,109 --> 00:40:08,433
That kind of scared me.

654
00:40:11,825 --> 00:40:14,000
But I still wanted to be with you.

655
00:40:15,345 --> 00:40:19,125
Yet being with you makes my love overflow,

656
00:40:19,125 --> 00:40:23,021
and just when I thought
I couldn't handle it anymore,

657
00:40:23,021 --> 00:40:25,333
you told me you loved me.

658
00:40:28,417 --> 00:40:32,766
It might trouble you,
and it might be selfish,

659
00:40:33,385 --> 00:40:35,177
but I'm going to say it.

660
00:40:38,237 --> 00:40:41,169
I love you, Mr. Seo.

661
00:40:54,829 --> 00:40:56,657
You know

662
00:40:57,861 --> 00:41:00,141
this is what Mizuki Seo said.

663
00:41:01,973 --> 00:41:04,183
Saying "I love you" to someone

664
00:41:04,853 --> 00:41:07,321
makes that person invincible.

665
00:41:09,321 --> 00:41:11,421
And just now,

666
00:41:11,421 --> 00:41:14,133
when you said that you love me,
that's how I felt.

667
00:41:15,101 --> 00:41:17,105
Like there's nothing to be afraid of.

668
00:41:17,105 --> 00:41:19,245
Like I'm truly invincible.

669
00:41:20,597 --> 00:41:24,633
And because I'm invincible,
I can do anything.

670
00:41:24,633 --> 00:41:29,545
And no matter how huge of a burden I hold,
I won't let anything spill over.

671
00:41:29,545 --> 00:41:31,549
I'll carry it all.

672
00:41:31,549 --> 00:41:35,033
Love is amazing. Being invincible is amazing.

673
00:41:37,485 --> 00:41:41,709
So, I'm going to make you
invincible too, O-Con.

674
00:41:43,585 --> 00:41:48,900
I love you...

675
00:41:55,045 --> 00:41:56,905
I love you.

676
00:41:57,573 --> 00:42:00,711
I love you, Mr. Seo!

677
00:42:00,711 --> 00:42:03,005
Hey...

678
00:42:05,621 --> 00:42:07,633
Yes! I win!

679
00:42:14,393 --> 00:42:17,617
I love you! I love you, O-Con!

680
00:42:17,617 --> 00:42:19,029
I love how you're almost always mad

681
00:42:19,029 --> 00:42:21,665
and how cute you are singing
in the dark when you're down!

682
00:42:21,665 --> 00:42:23,533
I love everything! Alright, I win!

683
00:42:23,533 --> 00:42:27,461
What? Well, in that case,
I love how much you love your grandma!

684
00:42:27,461 --> 00:42:29,333
And I love how pathetic
and quick to cry you are!

685
00:42:29,333 --> 00:42:31,393
Love you, love you, love you,
love you, love you!

686
00:42:31,393 --> 00:42:34,505
Love you! Love, love, love, love,
love, love, love, love, love!

687
00:42:34,505 --> 00:42:36,180
- Ten loves!
- Me too!

688
00:42:36,180 --> 00:42:39,745
Love, love, love, love, love, love,
love, love, love, times 10 to the 10th.

689
00:42:39,745 --> 00:42:41,933
Times 10... I lose! Alright!

690
00:42:41,933 --> 00:42:44,513
- Love, love... Ten!
- Ten... That's a tie.

691
00:42:44,513 --> 00:42:46,905
<i>Do people really say "I love you" that much?</i>

692
00:42:46,905 --> 00:42:50,405
- They've been keeping it bottled up.
- Marriage! Marriage! Love!

693
00:42:52,545 --> 00:42:56,425
These are theatrical tears.

694
00:42:56,425 --> 00:43:00,021
- Go! Don't grab!
- Love!

695
00:43:00,021 --> 00:43:02,781
- I said I love you!
- Yes!

696
00:43:04,425 --> 00:43:07,521
- So cute!
- I made friends!

697
00:43:07,521 --> 00:43:09,881
- So cute.
- So cute.

698
00:43:09,881 --> 00:43:12,209
Super cute!

699
00:43:12,209 --> 00:43:14,605
- Cute.
- So cute.

700
00:43:14,605 --> 00:43:16,229
Cute.

701
00:43:16,229 --> 00:43:18,800
- I love it.
- I love it.

702
00:43:23,553 --> 00:43:26,413
So cute! I love this!

703
00:43:26,413 --> 00:43:28,545
- So cute.
- I love it.

704
00:43:28,545 --> 00:43:30,581
Love it! I love this!

705
00:43:37,529 --> 00:43:39,401
I love it!

706
00:43:39,401 --> 00:43:41,593
<i>How do you feel about being chosen
as a new member?</i>

707
00:43:41,593 --> 00:43:47,617
<i>Well, I've been studying under
the two of them all this time,</i>

708
00:43:47,617 --> 00:43:50,800
<i>so I'm truly thrilled.</i>

709
00:43:50,800 --> 00:43:52,733
<i>I look forward to working with you.</i>

710
00:43:52,733 --> 00:43:55,913
<i>Yes! I'll give it my best muscle!</i>

711
00:43:55,913 --> 00:43:57,193
Oh, my.

712
00:43:57,193 --> 00:44:00,122
- <i>Okay.</i>
- I love it!

713
00:44:00,122 --> 00:44:01,433
[Cynical Molco
and Full Tummy Molco: The Movie]

714
00:44:01,433 --> 00:44:02,433
[Two Hearts Connected by Tuesla]
Cute!

715
00:44:02,433 --> 00:44:04,929
- Wow, so cute!
- Cute!

716
00:44:04,929 --> 00:44:07,966
One more...

717
00:44:07,966 --> 00:44:09,645
- Okay!
- Yes, look over here!

718
00:44:09,645 --> 00:44:12,700
- Ready? Say, "Love!"
- Love!

719
00:44:12,700 --> 00:44:14,533
- Love!
- Love!

720
00:44:14,533 --> 00:44:16,621
- Cute!
- So cute!

721
00:44:16,621 --> 00:44:18,893
- Thank you very much.
- How about this one?

722
00:44:28,569 --> 00:44:30,373
How is it?

723
00:44:31,993 --> 00:44:34,149
Delicious.

724
00:44:34,149 --> 00:44:35,429
I love this.

725
00:44:35,429 --> 00:44:37,225
I see.

726
00:44:51,700 --> 00:44:53,966
I love it.

727
00:45:15,893 --> 00:45:19,717
I love Tuesla.

728
00:45:21,013 --> 00:45:23,458
- I'm truly grateful.
- Yeah!

729
00:45:26,869 --> 00:45:28,629
I love it.

730
00:45:56,065 --> 00:46:01,476
[The End]
